# Non-secret release settings: the public domain baked into the web app. Read
# by infra/scripts/ship.sh (the `just deploy` driver), infra/scripts/
# remote-release.sh (on the builder) and infra/scripts/build-push.sh. An
# environment variable of the same name wins. Where a release is built and
# where it runs (NARRATIVE_BUILDER, NARRATIVE_VM: ssh targets on a private
# network) live in the private overlay, private/release.env, in the same
# KEY=value form; ship.sh reads that first. Secrets never live in either;
# production reads its own infra/.env.prod on the VM.

# Public domain: where ship.sh and remote-release.sh check /version.json after a
# deploy. The images do not depend on it (the web app uses /api and /ws).
DOMAIN=narrative.bastla.com
